module j3.thread — Threads, locks, a blocking queue, and a worker pool (pthreads on Linux, Win32 threads and SRW locks on Windows; the OS layer is `j3.threadsys`).

fn: cores spawn join
struct Thread: tid f arg name
struct Mutex: w0 w1 w2 w3 w4 lock() unlock() tryLock()
struct Cond: w0 w1 w2 w3 w4 w5 wait() signal() broadcast()
struct Queue: m notEmpty notFull items head len closed create() put() take() push() tryPush() pop()
    tryPop() count() close()
struct Job: f arg
struct Pool: jobs threads ranges pending m idle create() submit() trySubmit() submitBoxed()
    pendingJobs() finished() wait() parallelFor() parallelForEach() shutdown()

signatures and comments: `j3c doc j3.thread`; one name: `j3c doc j3.thread <name>`
